// Title: Potential Signing Bypass Via Windows Developer Features - Registry
// Sigma ID: b110ebaf-697f-4da1-afd5-b536fa27a2c1
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-01-12 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: stealth
// Description: Detects when the enablement of developer features such as "Developer Mode" or "Application
//   Sideloading". Which allows the user to install untrusted packages.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/malmoeb/status/1560536653709598721
//   - https://www.sentinelone.com/labs/inside-malicious-windows-apps-for-malware-deployment/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_turn_on_dev_features.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 1 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (RegistryKey contains "\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\AppModelUnlock" or RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Appx.*$") and (RegistryKey endswith "\\AllowAllTrustedApps" or RegistryKey endswith "\\AllowDevelopmentWithoutDevLicense") and RegistryValueData =~ "DWORD (0x00000001)"
